redfin 1196: keybag status events (0xe3ffd00d) so SpringBoard sees the passcode and locks; kern.sweet_passcode_notify

1195 on r5tid1: passcode set fine, but the lock screen never asked and aks_lock_device (sel 8/32) was never
called. SpringBoard's SBFMobileKeyBag reads the keybag state at init and then only on MobileKeyBag events:
MKBEventsRegister adds an IOGeneralInterest notification on AppleKeyStore and aksNotificationCB maps message
0xe3ffd00d to "keybag status changed" (-> _queue_handleKeybagStatusChanged: lockStateExtended,
setHasPasscodeIfNecessary) and 0xe3ffd00f to "first unlock". We never sent either, so SpringBoard kept its
boot-time "no passcode" state (and Settings showed "on" only after re-entering the pane).
Now AppleKeyStore messageClients(0xe3ffd00d) on: passcode set/removed, lock, unlock, failed attempt, reset,
and every kern.sweet_passcode change (so recovery to 0 drops SpringBoard's passcode state at once).
All senders are in the passcode code paths: nothing is sent while kern.sweet_passcode stays 0.
kern.sweet_passcode_notify (root, mode != 0): 1 = send an event, 2 = lock now (+ event).
kern.sweet_passcode_state gains events=N.

